{
 "_about": "EVERY ACTION, ONE ROW EACH (owner, 17 Nov). `name` is what a phone posts (or `?run=` names, with `run: true`); `handler` the backend function it reaches; `roles` the permission tiers that may (anyone = signed out, member = signed in, child, admin; a tier's roles are settings.json `roles`); `feature` listed in the payload's `features` so a phone can tell what this deploy can do; `arg` a job that takes `&arg=`. A handler still checks WHOSE row it is — the gate only checks who is signed in. `node tools/permissions.js` writes ACTION_ACCESS and RUNNABLE (access.gs), postActions_ (dopost.gs), payloadFeatures_ (get-start.gs), PERMISSIONS (booking.gs) and permissions.json from this; edit here, never there.",
